# API keys for the metadata providers that need an account.
#
# Copy this to `.env` and fill in whichever you have. `.env` is gitignored: keys
# are never compiled into the binary and never committed. VuIO reads `.env` from
# its config directory first, then the working directory, and a real environment
# variable always wins over the file — so a systemd unit, a Docker `-e` flag or a
# shell export work just as well and need no file at all.
#
# A provider with no key is skipped rather than failing: it is off, not broken.
# Nothing here is read until `[mediainfo] enabled = true` and a fetch is run.
#
# A key can also be set per-server from the MediaInfo tab in either web
# interface. That stores it in the database and takes precedence over anything
# here; clearing it there falls back to these.
#
# The variable is always VUIO_<PROVIDER ID>_API_KEY, whatever the provider calls
# the credential itself.

# --- Movies and TV -----------------------------------------------------------

# TheMovieDB — movies, TV, posters, trailers and ratings.
# https://developer.themoviedb.org
VUIO_TMDB_API_KEY=

# OMDb — IMDb ratings, posters and plot summaries.
# https://omdbapi.com
VUIO_OMDB_API_KEY=

# --- Music -------------------------------------------------------------------

# Discogs — vinyl, CD and master releases, and artist discographies.
# Wants a personal access token. https://www.discogs.com/settings/developers
VUIO_DISCOGS_API_KEY=

# Last.fm — artist biographies, tags and album art.
# https://www.last.fm/api/account/create
VUIO_LASTFM_API_KEY=

# Genius — lyrics and song credits. Wants an access token.
# https://genius.com/api-clients
VUIO_GENIUS_API_KEY=

# TVmaze, MusicBrainz, Jikan, AniList and Kitsu need no account and are on by
# default, so they have nothing to configure here.
